<article class="env-lemma" id="07NG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07NG">Lemma <span data-tag="07NG">10.164.4</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R \to S$ is faithfully flat, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S$ is a regular ring. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $R$ is a regular ring. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We see that $R$ is Noetherian by Lemma <a href="/tag/033E" data-tag="033E">10.164.1</a>. Let $\mathfrak p \subset R$ be a prime. Choose a prime $\mathfrak q \subset S$ lying over $\mathfrak p$. Then Lemma <a href="/tag/00OF" data-tag="00OF">10.110.9</a> applies to $R_\mathfrak p \to S_\mathfrak q$ and we conclude that $R_\mathfrak p$ is regular. Since $\mathfrak p$ was arbitrary we see $R$ is regular. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>